        {
          "title": "TEST 23.09",
          "description": "https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScyBp9KqmdRPsyfvv1DneplwcZB2Ui1MpdNI3nV-JFhkUC_4A/viewform?usp=sf_link",
          "attachments": [],
          "answers": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Добре 🙂 давай зробимо по черзі.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Definitions\n\nТреба співставити слова з правильними значеннями. Два визначення зайві:\n\n* uncover → Remove a cover or covering from something.\n* details → Small features, facts or parts of something.\n* prehistoric → Relating to or about the period thousands of years ago before written records.\n* ancient → Belonging to the very distant past and no longer in existence.\n* giant → Very very very big.\n* site → An area of ground on which a town, building, or monument is built.\n* erect → Build or put up a building, wall, or other upright structure.\n* supply → To give somebody what is lacking or needed.\n\n❌ Зайві:\n\n* \"Something that is difficult or impossible to understand or explain\"\n* \"To produce something new, which did exist before\"\n\n---\n\n### 2. Fill in the gaps\n\n1. details\n2. all\n3. been\n4. away\n5. site\n6. date\n7. giant\n8. burial\n9. the\n10. erect\n11. not\n12. too\n\n---\n\n### 3. True or False\n\n* Scientists know the names of the people who built Stonehenge. → False\n* The ancient stones are in the southeast of England. → False (they are in the southwest)\n* Scientists believe Stonehenge's architects are Welsh and not English. → True\n* The oldest human remains found at Stonehenge are 3,000 years old. → False (≈ 5,000 years old)\n* Each stone at Stonehenge is four metres wide. → False (4 m high, 2.1 m wide)\n* Scientists don't know how the stones got from Wales to Stonehenge. → True\n* The people who transported the stones may be buried at Stonehenge. → True\n* The stones that make up Stonehenge are bluestones. → True\n\n---\n\n### 4. Past tenses\n\n1. He wanted to repair our washing machine that had broken a few days before.\n2. Before he rang at my door, he had been looking for a parking space for about ten minutes.\n3. Suddenly, I realised that they were showing our street on TV.\n4. The reporter said that a car had crashed into a stop sign just before reaching the crossroads.\n5. I opened the door and saw a police officer standing there.\n6. He was waiting for the plumber the whole day.\n7. As it turned out, it was our plumber’s car that had rolled down the street.\n8. Before he had turned 25, he never left his native town.\n9. I probably lost my key when I was running in the park.\n\n---\n\nХочеш, я зроблю для тебе готові варіанти відповідей у вигляді таблиці (щоб можна було зручно вставити у роботу)?",
              "local_path": null
            }
